en-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Araki</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Meguro</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Masaki</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kumanishi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Arakawa</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mishina</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular diversity of the NMDA receptor channel</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1992</year><volume>358</volume><fpage>36</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1377365</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/358036a0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Loftis</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Janowsky</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The N-methyl-D-aspartate receptor subunit NR2B: localization, functional properties, regulation, and clinical implications</article-title><source>Pharmacol Ther</source><year>2003</year><volume>97</volume><fpage>55</fpage><lpage>85</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12493535</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0163-7258(02)00302-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Monyer</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Sprengel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Schoepfer</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Herb</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Higuchi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lomeli</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Burnashev</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakmann</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Seeburg</surna